ETE runs while requiring open-PR worktrees to be skipped unconditionally; AC10:183–185 repeats that protection. The plan does not establish how those other candidates are protected when PR state cannot be obtained. Define refusal or skipping when open-PR status cannot be established, and cover that case in R10.","id":"F3"},{"blocking":true,"document":"requirements/spec.md","evidence":"The rubric contradicts explicit exceptions. AC10:182 permits non-interactive removal for empty lists, and R10:210 includes that behavior in Pass, but its Fail condition rejects any removal without confirmation. AC9:168–170 preserves existing push denials, while R9:209 fails whenever a push is denied. State the non-interactive confirmation exception and limit R9's denial failure to a denial introduced solely because reviews have not converged.","id":"F4"},{"blocking":true,"document":"requirements/spec.md","evidence":"AC3:81–82 and R3:203 say low findings never block. AC6:116–118 requires regressions of the previous fix to block in rounds 4–5 without a severity exception; plan.md:104–105 repeats this. A low-severity regression therefore has contradictory required outcomes. Define precedence consistently in the criteria, plan and rubric, with an explicit test for that intersection.","id":"F5"}],"kind":"planning-review","mandate":{"constraints":["Stay within the approved design.md and spec.md and the plan.md and issues.md derived from them.","Do not merge the final PR into main and do not build, tag or publish a release; those need the human's separate instruction.","Do not weaken existing GateReeve proof, review, protection or mandate obligations.","Run hosted CI only after a slice's paired reviews converge; iterate review rounds on local commits with local verification."],"goal":"Implement the approved tb-convergence-and-retirement design and spec (AC1-AC11) as six slice PRs into the tb-convergence-and-retirement integration branch, and deliver a ready, unmerged final PR into main."},"mandateAssessment":{"evidence":"The six-slice delivery, local review rounds and unmerged final PR match the human's grant and mandate (requirements/plan.md:20–31). However, AC9 and P8 omit the approved design's requirement that CI qualification cover the local receipts consumed by reviewers. Substituting tree identity and passing required checks alone weakens the mandated proof obligations.","outcome":"FAIL"},"outcome":"FAIL","output":{"bytes":3170,"format":"json","hash":"sha256:12b9baf444ec343e9a426208e171f92a41076c02384d2bb4a8b9f7a619190d9a"},"receipt":{"bytes":1349,"format":"json","hash":"sha256:8e20748ac308c6e61f84ab97d476340ec13a7a9a9c41564416d1ce6ff1ae5053"},"reviewContract":"sha256:175e6f5dc6869ee5480441e98393d75d9f272edd164c441337fbcb339440aabd","runId":"tb-convergence-and-retirement-start-linux-1","subject":"sha256:aca8cf5e1632dbcac1d5b7e98b764dfcd42c95505f3799d4f308d5ee515b730a","summary":"Implementation authorization is blocked by weakened CI qualification, missing inhibitor-refusal behavior, unresolved sweep safety, and contradictory acceptance and rubric conditions."}